          "path": "_m/9/q/8/z/san-francisco-bay-area-wp/muir-woods-national-monument-4.jpg",
          "filename": "Muir Woods National Monument (46966706055).jpg",
          "caption": "Muir Woods National Monument is part of California’s Golden Gate National Recreation Area, north of San Francisco. It’s known for its towering old-growth redwood trees. Trails wind among the trees to Cathedral Grove and Bohemian Grove, and along Redwood Creek. The Ben Johnson and Dipsea trails climb a hillside for views of the treetops, the Pacific Ocean and Mount Tamalpais in adjacent Mount Tamalpais State Park.",
          "alt": "Muir Woods National Monument is part of California’s Golden Gate National Recreation Area, north of San Francisco. It’s known for its towering old-growth redwood trees. Trails wind among the trees to Cathedral Grove and Bohemian Grove, and along Redwood Creek. The Ben Johnson and Dipsea trails climb a hillside for views of the treetops, the Pacific Ocean and Mount Tamalpais in adjacent Mount Tamalpais State Park.",
          "width": 3000,
          "height": 2250,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Matthew Dillon from Hollywood, CA, USA",
